<p>Robstown sits about 15 miles west of downtown Corpus Christi along SH 44 and US 77, surrounded by the cotton, grain, and sorghum farms of western Nueces County. As a public adjuster in Robstown, TX, we help homeowners, farmers, and business owners with wind, hail, tornado, and water damage claims. Corpus Christi Public Adjuster serves Robstown and nearby Banquete, Driscoll, Petronila, and Agua Dulce from the Corpus Christi area. We do not have a Robstown office; we come to your property.</p>
<p>Inland Nueces County has a different risk profile than the islands. Storm surge is not the main concern here. Instead, squall lines and supercells crossing open farmland can produce violent straight-line winds and large hail. Robstown's housing includes older pier-and-beam and wood-frame homes, brick homes on slabs, manufactured homes, and rural properties with barns, equipment sheds, and metal shop buildings. Those metal buildings, carports, and older roofs are often the first to show damage.</p>

